From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:38:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: Let MXXMLWriter write into a document, building it as
 the events come.

An MXXMLWriter whose output is a DOM document is what Click-to-Run builds
the configuration of Office's App-V layer with, and put_output() refused
a document.  What Windows does is in msxml6's test_mxwriter_domdoc,
whose todo_wine lines now all pass: startDocument() empties the document
and locks it -- createNode() fails until endDocument() -- startElement()
puts the element into the tree at once, and text shows up when its
element ends.  Comments, processing instructions and CDATA sections from
the lexical handler become nodes too; that part is not yet measured on
Windows.

The reader writing into the writer, from the old tree's tests, passes,
and so do the old tree's newline cases for MXXMLWriter40.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/msxml3/domdoc.c b/dlls/msxml3/domdoc.c
